<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    updatePeriodMillis is 0 on purpose. Android's own widget refresh cannot be
    asked for anything under thirty minutes, and it wakes the device to deliver
    it — which for this widget would be both too coarse and too expensive: the
    countdown is a Chronometer, so it runs on its own with no process alive at
    all, and the only moments the rest of the face has to change are the six
    marks of the day. The provider sets an alarm for exactly those. See
    PrayerWidgetProvider.scheduleBoundary.

    The heights below were raised when the pane was rebuilt to the card's own
    proportions, and they were raised because they had become a lie. Added up
    from the layout, at the app's own spacing scale:

         24   the pane's own padding, top and bottom
         34   the head
         60   a 16 gap and the 44 disc under it
         17   a 16 gap and the rule
         58   a 12 gap and a strip cell
        ===
        193   everything but the note
        +44   a 12 gap, 16 of padding and a line of text
        ===
        237   in the sunrise gap

    The old 110dp was honest for the old face, which was three lines of text.
    It is not honest for this one, and a launcher takes minHeight at its word —
    at 110 it handed the pane two cells, the vertical LinearLayout ran out of
    room at the last child, and the strip was measured to nothing. Six times
    silently missing, which is the one thing this widget exists to show.

    minHeight is 195 and not 237, and the difference is the whole of what
    NOTE_NEEDS_DP is for: the face this widget must ALWAYS be able to draw is
    the one without the note, and that is 193. Asking for the taller number
    would be asking for room this pane only sometimes needs.

    It is also not a free number to raise. A launcher that cannot satisfy a
    grown minHeight on an already-placed copy does not resize it — Samsung's
    drops it off the home screen, and the reader loses a widget by installing an
    update. 195 clears the 193 it has to and stays under the ~198dp two cells
    come to on a common phone, so an existing copy survives. targetCellHeight
    asks for the third cell for NEW copies, where nothing is lost by asking.

    minResizeHeight is 180 rather than the old 80: below about that the strip
    starts losing its descenders, and a widget squeezed until the times are
    clipped is one whose only job has failed quietly.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="195dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="3"
    android:minResizeWidth="180dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="180dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/prayer_widget"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/prayer_widget"
    android:description="@string/prayer_widget_description"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0" />
